# Rules Generation

Generate supporting rules calibrated to lifecycle context.

## Rules by Context

AlwaysGenerateRules {
  rules/task-creator.mdc => @guidance/task-lifecycle.mdc
  rules/review.mdc => references all generated stack/pattern rules
  rules/tdd.mdc => @guidance/testing-methodology.mdc
}

RulesByContext {
  TeamTool+ => rules/log.mdc per @guidance/task-lifecycle.mdc#ActivityLogging
  MVP+ => rules/productmanager.mdc per @guidance/product-management.mdc
  BusinessRisk+ => rules/security.mdc per @guidance/security-patterns.mdc
}

## Generation Process

generateSupportingRules(lifecycle, risk) {
  For each in AlwaysGenerateRules => generate with L1-L2 calibration
  (lifecycle >= TeamTool) => generate RulesByContext[TeamTool+]
  (lifecycle >= MVP) => generate RulesByContext[MVP+]
  (risk >= Business) => generate RulesByContext[BusinessRisk+]
}

## Core Rule Generation

generateCore(choices) {
  Generate rules/core.mdc with:
    - RTC thinking pattern from @guidance/thinking-patterns.mdc
    - Behaviors calibrated per L1 lifecycle
    - Constraints derived from L2 params
    - Principle levels from @guidance/programming-principles.mdc
}

## Review Rule Special Case

generateReview(generatedRules) {
  Scan all generated rules/
  Build Criteria{} block referencing each
  Include OWASP checks if BusinessRisk+
  Reference security rules if generated
}

Constraints {
  Calibrate rule strictness to lifecycle.
  Reference guidance files, don't duplicate.
  Review rule must reference all other generated rules.
}
